- How handle hash collisions and index eviction?
- What telemetry would you collect for ROI without compromising privacy?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about cost-benefit tradeoffs for on-device prefetching and privacy-friendly design in a beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts
- On-device caching and prefetching strategies
- Resource budgets: energy, memory, data
- Privacy and consent controls
- Observability: cache hit rate, latency, drift
- Rollout strategy and break-even planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight prefetch example (pseudo)
async function prefetchAssets(urls, cache) {
  for (const u of urls) {
    try {
      const resp = await fetch(u, {mode: 'no-cors', credentials: 'omit'});
      if (resp.ok) await cache.put(u, resp.clone());
    } catch (e) { /* ignore */ }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure energy impact on mobile vs desktop?
- How would you ensure privacy compliance and opt-in UX for prefetching?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a lightweight edge optimization with clear cost/benefit trade-offs, focusing on data movement, energy, and privacy in mobile environments.

## Key Concepts

- Content-based fingerprinting
- Bloom filters for on-device dedup
- Bandwidth vs CPU energy trade-offs
- Privacy considerations and optional cloud verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: compute hash and check Bloom filter
function canSend(record, bloom) {
  const h = hash(record); // deterministic fingerprint
  if (bloom.mightContain(h)) return false;
  bloom.add(h);
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you estimate Bloom filter false positive rate given device memory constraints?
- How would you rollout to mitigate drift in data patterns and ensure continued value?

## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests the ability to quantify a data-heavy feature with a clear offline-first constraint, balancing device resources against business value.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first architectures
- Local indexing and delta synchronization
- Resource budgeting (CPU, memory, storage)
- Data transfer costs and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```
// Implementation sketch: simple local search index
class LocalIndex {
  constructor() { this.docs = []; }
  build(docs) { this.docs = docs.map(d => ({ id: d.id, text: d.content })); }
  search(q) {
    const terms = q.toLowerCase().split(/\s+/);
    return this.docs.filter(d => terms.every(t => d.text.toLowerCase().includes(t)));
  }
  deltaUpdate(changes) {
    // apply lightweight patches to docs
    changes.forEach(c => {
      const idx = this.docs.findIndex(d => d.id === c.id);
      if (idx >= 0) this.docs[idx] = { ...this.docs[idx], ...c.patch };
      else this.docs.push({ id: c.id, text: c.patch.content });
    });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement delta-sync to minimize data transfer while ensuring consistency?
- What privacy controls would you layer to protect sensitive docs during offline usage?

## Why This Is Asked

